Scenario: briefTest1 | model.User creates a brief without an explicit brief ID
GIVEN user creates a model.Brief with mission ID 1, title "t1", date "1990-12-30", and content "con1"
WHEN the model.Brief object is initialized
THEN the brief's ID is -1, and it contains the expected mission ID, title, date, and content

Scenario: briefTest2 | model.User creates a brief with an explicit brief ID
GIVEN user creates a model.Brief with brief ID 25, mission ID 1, title "t1", date "1990-12-30", and content "con1"
WHEN the model.Brief object is initialized
THEN the brief contains the expected brief ID, mission ID, title, date, and content

Scenario: invalidDateTest | model.User creates a brief with an invalid date format
GIVEN user creates a model.Brief with mission ID 1, title "t1", date "22222-25-30", and content "con1"
WHEN the model.Brief object is initialized
THEN an IllegalArgumentException is thrown

Scenario: invalidDateTest2 | model.User creates a brief with a date using slashes instead of hyphens
GIVEN user creates a model.Brief with mission ID 1, title "t1", date "1990/12/02", and content "con1"
WHEN the model.Brief object is initialized
